                <pb facs="0326" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg238"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Squiers.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-03-01"><hi rendition="#italic">March 1,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 347.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 853, of the 12th ultimo, regarding the outrage on the United States
                    consulate at Cienfuegos.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to say that in view of the apologies made and the precautions
                    taken to prevent a repetition of the insult, the Department is of opinion that
                    the incident may be regarded as closed. * * *</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
